From 1ae0925697336707d239d2b26016072402a8f091 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 01:13:05 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] docs: de-Beads sweep + 6-stage onboarding consistency for
 0.1.0

Aligns onboarding/reference docs to the canonical 6 workflow stages
(/plan /dev /validate /ship /review /verify) with pre-merge as an
embedded gate, and reframes docs kernel-first with Beads as an opt-out
backend.

- Phantom /premerge + stage count (kernel cb70c04a): fix the taught flow
  in QUICKSTART, MIGRATION, MANUAL_REVIEW_GUIDE, TEMPLATES, TOOLCHAIN
  (ref + consumer copy); AGENTS.md "7 named stage skills" -> "6 workflow
  stages + composable research skill" reconciled with its 6-row table.
- ENHANCED_ONBOARDING demotion (cb70c04a): moved from Tutorials to
  Historical in docs/INDEX.md + superseded-by-QUICKSTART banner (not
  rewritten).
- Docs de-Beads sweep (kernel 5021a1f8): SETUP.md + TOOLCHAIN.md now
  present the kernel backend as the zero-install default and Beads as
  opt-out/migration; corrected the false claim that project memory
  requires bd (lib/project-memory.js is kernel-backed via kernel_memories
  / sqlite-driver, zero bd calls); AGENTS.md "Beads issue" -> "issue".
- Root CLAUDE.md reduced to a thin @AGENTS.md pointer; still-relevant
  build/shell/MCP/git-hook content moved into AGENTS.md (stale Beads
  lines dropped in the move).
- Regenerated D20 bd call-site kill-list artifact so `release check
  --target 0.1.0` stays 0 blockers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
